%N A037743 Decimal expansion of a(n) is given by the first n terms of the periodic sequence with initial period 2,1,3,0.
%H A037743 <a href="/index/Rec#order_05">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (10,0,0,1,-10).
%F A037743 From _R. J. Mathar_, Oct 05 2009: (Start)
%F A037743 a(n) = 10*a(n-1) + a(n-4) - 10*a(n-5).
%F A037743 G.f.: x*(2+x+3*x^2) / ((x-1)*(10*x-1)*(1+x)*(x^2+1)). (End)
%F A037743 a(n) = floor(71*10^(n+1)/3333). - _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Sep 23 2026
%F A037743 E.g.f.: (-606*exp(-x) - 1111*exp(x) + 1420*exp(10*x) + 297*cos(x) - 363*sin(x))/6666. - _Stefano Spezia_, Sep 23 2026
%t A037743 Table[FromDigits[PadRight[{},n,{2,1,3,0}]],{n,20}] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Feb 24 2025 *)
%o A037743 (PARI) Vec(x*(2+x+3*x^2)/((x-1)*(10*x-1)*(1+x)*(x^2+1)) + O(x^25)) \\ _Jinyuan Wang_, Apr 14 2020
%K A037743 nonn,base,easy,changed
